{"org":"elastic","repo":"elasticsearch","prNumber":"113272","commit":"f93cf80dc1d131dbaf65ea1876f76c908bf3c65b","generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The `name` argument passed to `addSuppliers` already contains angle brackets (e.g., `\"\u003cno alt geo_point\u003e\"`, `\"\u003cwith alt cartesian_point\u003e\"`). Since `addSuppliers` wraps the name in its own brackets (`\"\u003csingle \" + name + \"\u003e\"` and `\"\u003c\" + name + \"s\u003e\"`), the resulting supplier names become awkwardly nested: `\"\u003csingle \u003cno alt geo_point\u003e\u003e\"` and `\"\u003cno alt geo_point\u003es\u003e\"`.\nAll other call sites pass plain names like `\"0 int\"`, `\"positive double\"`, `\"random boolean\"`, producing clean results like `\"\u003csingle 0 int\u003e\"` / `\"\u003c0 ints\u003e\"`. For consistency, the geo and cartesian point names should drop the embedded brackets, e.g. `\"no alt geo_point\"` and `\"with alt geo_point\"`, yielding `\"\u003csingle no alt geo_point\u003e\"` / `\"\u003cno alt geo_points\u003e\"`.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/MultiRowTestCaseSupplier.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/MultiRowTestCaseSupplier.java-15761:15782,16107:16130,16158:16241-12371:12588,12630:12876","promptId":"#ART37","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/MultiRowTestCaseSupplier.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/MultiRowTestCaseSupplier.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":15761,"endPos":15782,"startLine":420,"startLineOffset":16,"endLine":420,"endLineOffset":37,"length":22},{"pos":16107,"endPos":16130,"startLine":431,"startLineOffset":20,"endLine":431,"endLineOffset":43,"length":24},{"pos":16158,"endPos":16241,"startLine":432,"startLineOffset":26,"endLine":432,"endLineOffset":109,"length":84}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":12371,"endPos":12588,"startLi